herolte: the PMU step of deep idle that Samsung's Linux does before the SMC (0441)

min70: no breadcrumb at all, so the core never reached the entry; CPU_ON said it was OFF. Reading Samsung's open kernel (LineageOS android_kernel_samsung_universal8890, drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-powermode.c and exynos-pmu.c): enter_c2() calls exynos_cpu.power_down(cpu) first, which clears the local power bits (0xf) of the core's PMU CONFIGURATION register (PMU base 0x105c0000 + 0x2000 + 0x80 * (Aff1 << 2 | Aff0)); only then the PSCI call. We had only the SMC. 0441: the idle path clears those bits before CPU_SUSPEND and restores them if the call returns; the registers are mapped by the power thread when deep idle is armed (no mapping, no deep idle) and CONFIG/STATUS of all cores are logged (read only); the watchdog restores 0xf before its CPU_ON. heroidle only (D-0089).

